"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"verifier_lab_execution_spine","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[verifier_lab_execution_spine].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"verifier_lab_kernel","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[verifier_lab_kernel].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"voice_to_doctrine_self_improvement_loop","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[voice_to_doctrine_self_improvement_loop].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"world_model_projection_drift_control_room","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[world_model_projection_drift_control_room].axiom_refs"}],"cited_by_count":35,"component_ids":["bounded_autonomy_campaign_packet","bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","cognitive_operator_registry","cold_reader_route_map","concurrency_mission_control","corpus_readiness_mathlib_absence_gate","engine_room_demo","finance_forecast_evaluation_spine","formal_evidence_cell_anchor_resolver","formal_math_premise_retrieval","formal_math_readiness_gate","formal_math_verifier_trace_repair_loop","lean_std_premise_index","materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","prediction_oracle_reconciliation","proof_diagnostic_evidence_spine","provider_context_recipe_budget_policy","public_reveal_walkthrough","research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","ring2_premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness","routing_anti_patterns_registry","self_ignorance_coverage_ledger","spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","tool_server_pressure_inventory","undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","verifier_lab_execution_spine","verifier_lab_kernel","voice_to_doctrine_self_improvement_loop","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":["AP-6"],"id":"AX-7","kind":"axiom","plain":"Formal clause: a partial computation `g` is totalized as `Result`: `Ok(y)` when `Pre(x)` holds, otherwise `Refusal(reason,evidence)`.","principles":["P-8"],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The cash machine only stands for operations that were built to decline; operations without that check can still hand out a wrong amount.","maps":[{"analogy":"what the machine needs to release cash, such as enough balance and a reachable account","doctrine":"the precondition that must hold for a real result"},{"analogy":"the machine dispensing the amount requested","doctrine":"returning a value when the precondition holds"},{"analogy":"the printed slip saying why it declined","doctrine":"a labelled refusal with a reason and evidence"},{"analogy":"never an arbitrary stack of cash you would take as a real withdrawal","doctrine":"never an unexplained number or NaN passed on"}],"text":"A cash machine that cannot complete a withdrawal prints the reason it declined and gives you no money. It never hands out some arbitrary amount instead."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A statistics routine divides by a sample size that is too small, returns the resulting NaN as a score, and a later page prints it as a real forecast.","does_not_prove":"Only the calculations that declare and check their preconditions return refusals; any other calculation can still return a bad value.","enforced_in_component_ids":["finance_forecast_evaluation_spine","corpus_readiness_mathlib_absence_gate"],"example":{"component_ids":["finance_forecast_evaluation_spine"],"text":"The finance forecast evaluation spine returns a labelled refusal naming the reason when a forecast horizon is at or above the sample size, or when the statistics library needed for a t-distribution is not installed, instead of returning a number computed outside its valid range."},"governs":"What a calculation may return when the conditions it needs do not hold.","plain":"A calculation may return a number only when the conditions it needs actually hold. When they don't, it hands back a labelled refusal naming the reason, never a quiet number or blank that the next step reads as an answer.","potential_misread":"That a number coming out at the end means the conditions were met, so a value can be used without checking that the calculation had what it needed.","refuses":"Returning a number or a NaN when the conditions for computing it were never checked.","requires":"A declared precondition for returning a value, and a labelled refusal with a reason and evidence on every other path, including missing libraries and undefined values.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"A missing input or an out-of-range condition shows up as a visible gap, instead of a plausible figure that a later page prints as a real result."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"AXIOMS.md::AX-7","statement":"Formal clause: a partial computation `g` is totalized as `Result`: `Ok(y)` when\n`Pre(x)` holds, otherwise `Refusal(reason,evidence)`.\n\nLineage: partial functions, domain theory, Result/Maybe types.\n\nRoute: recorded as strongly witnessed by `finance_forecast_evaluation_spine`,\n`corpus_readiness_mathlib_absence_gate`, the metabolism runtime and the finance\nstatistics modules. The tests require a typed refusal for an invalid forecast\nhorizon, for missing SciPy support, and for a claim that Mathlib is available\nwhen it is not.\n\nAnti-axiom: a computation given invalid input still returns a number, or a\nsilent NaN.","statement_sha256":"4c49321c15e70152e8bf3c92903a82a37e2d99fc9ae410c390eb701f3066c807","title":"Typed partiality and refusal","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}